<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  ============================================================================
  com.apple.SetupAssistant.managed  —  SkipSetupItems

  WHAT THIS IS
  The managed-preference form of Apple's SkipSetupItems setting. Normally an
  MDM delivers this as a configuration profile with PayloadType
  com.apple.ManagedClient.preferences, and ManagedClient unwraps it onto disk at

      /Library/Managed Preferences/com.apple.SetupAssistant.managed.plist

  This file IS that on-disk result. We write it directly because we cannot use
  MDM: Setup Assistant runs at first login, before enrollment, and enrollment is
  the thing we are trying to achieve. Writing it by hand requires SIP disabled,
  which the staging pipeline already does for the TCC grants.

  Pattern reference: rtrouton/profiles SkipWelcomeToMacSetup.mobileconfig, which
  does the same thing via MDM but only skips "Welcome".

  WHY WE NEED IT
  On a fresh AMI boot, per-user Setup Assistant ("Buddy") presents a nine-pane
  wizard and runs FRONTMOST as com.apple.SetupAssistant. Verified via lsappinfo:
  System Settings sat at list position 49 while Buddy held the foreground, so
  cliclick's physical clicks landed on Buddy and enrollment failed 16 times at
  "Install button not found". One pane is an Apple ID sign-in we have no account
  for, so it cannot be answered headlessly.

  Note that "tell application settingsApp to activate" does NOT beat Buddy.
  That was tested and it does not work.

  KEY LIST
  Values below were extracted from the Setup Assistant binary on macOS 27.0.1
  (strings on /System/Library/CoreServices/Setup Assistant.app) and
  cross-checked against Apple's documented SkipSetupItems vocabulary.
  Unrecognised keys are ignored, so a superset is safe and forward-compatible.

  Deliberately EXCLUDED: the Organization* keys (OrganizationName,
  OrganizationAddress and friends). Those are Automated Device Enrollment
  profile fields, not skip items, and have no meaning here.

  KNOWN GAP — LIQUID GLASS
  The Liquid Glass / glass tint pane has NO skip key. The binary contains
  GlassSelection, GlassSelectionFlowItem, GlassSelectionViewController and
  LastSeenGlassTintUpsellProductVersion, but no matching entry in the skip-key
  vocabulary. So this file alone will still leave that one pane on screen.
  It is handled separately by pre-seeding com.apple.SetupAssistant for the user
  (LastSeenGlassTintUpsellProductVersion + SkipExpressSettingsUpdating).

  UNTESTED as of 2026-10-08. Written without a live box. Verify by checking the
  pane sequence on a fresh instance and by confirming the file survives the AMI
  snapshot. See memory: project-macos27-disk-unlock-prompt,
  project-macos27-enrollment-test.
  ============================================================================
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>SkipSetupItems</key>
	<array>
		<string>Accessibility</string>
		<string>AppStore</string>
		<string>Appearance</string>
		<string>AppleID</string>
		<string>ApplePay</string>
		<string>Biometric</string>
		<string>DeviceToDeviceMigration</string>
		<string>Diagnostics</string>
		<string>DisplayTone</string>
		<string>ExpressLanguage</string>
		<string>FileVault</string>
		<string>Intelligence</string>
		<string>Keyboards</string>
		<string>Location</string>
		<string>OSShowcase</string>
		<string>Payment</string>
		<string>PreferredLanguage</string>
		<string>Privacy</string>
		<string>Registration</string>
		<string>Restore</string>
		<string>RestoreCompleted</string>
		<string>ScreenSaver</string>
		<string>ScreenTime</string>
		<string>Siri</string>
		<string>SoftwareUpdate</string>
		<string>SpokenLanguage</string>
		<string>TOS</string>
		<string>TapToSetup</string>
		<string>TermsOfAddress</string>
		<string>TouchID</string>
